00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:05.269 align:start position:0%
the framework agreement follows weeks of  closed-door negotiations in the senate  it's one of the first bipartisan gun  control agreements in decades  we haven't had significant federal  legislation in nearly 30 years so having  a framework announced having 10  republican senators along with 10  democrats signing off on that which  would avoid the filibuster in the united  states senate it's a really big deal  the tentative agreement has been  welcomed by president biden who's  tweeted  i want to thank senator chris murphy and  the bipartisan group for the gun safety  proposal it does not do everything that  i think is needed but it reflects  important steps in the right direction  with bipartisan support there are no  excuses for delay let's get this done  but some don't want it done i think it's  deeply disappointing that republican  leadership decided to get in league with  the democratic conference in the senate  to put together a gun control bill  you know  that should be a huge red flag for  republican voters going into the fall  significant proposals include incentives  for states to pass so-called red flag  laws which allow a judge to decide  whether a gun buyer or owner poses a  potential threat to others  federal background checks on buyers  under 21 would include access to their  records as minors  and federal funding for mental health  care and increased school security  but these measures fall well short of  what's being demanded by gun control  advocates including president biden  himself  at rallies across the u.s saturday calls  were made for a ban on the sale of  semi-automatic weapons and high-capacity  magazines and for the age at which an  individual can buy a rifle to be raised  from 18 to 21 to match the existing  federal law concerning handguns  assault rifles were used in the mass  shootings in uvalvi texas and in buffalo  new york in each case they were wielded  by 18 year olds  the senators have set an informal goal  of passing the bill before the 24th of  this month when congress goes on a  two-week recess  but with the legislation still not fully  written it's unlikely that this goal  will be met  [Applause]  and it's certain that the modest  suggestions will do little to ease the  mounting pressure on politicians to pass  meaningful gun control measures  or face the consequences in november's  midterm elections  mike hanna al-jazeera washington
 

